{:event/id "e8f6b830-e4ce-4011-837b-72327b2996a2" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:fa5c14d5-c1dd-4779-a3f2-d0189d168caa" :event/seq 1 :event/causes ["fa5c14d5-c1dd-4779-a3f2-d0189d168caa"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:fa5c14d5-c1dd-4779-a3f2-d0189d168caa" :event/at "2026-09-09T13:49:36Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/mongo-temp-memory-round-trip-violates-expiry-field-codec :finding/shapes #{:store :law :representation} :finding/current-name "mongo-temp-memory set-memory!/get-memory!" :finding/candidate-name "KeyedTTLStore<Key,Value> (round-trip law violated)" :finding/claim "Mongo temp memory writes and TTL-indexes the field expiresAt, keywordizes Mongo documents without renaming fields, then reads :expires-at for application expiry validation. The persisted field therefore does not match the read-side field name at this revision, so a live stored document cannot satisfy the intended set-to-get round-trip. This is a representation-boundary failure, not evidence that generic TTL stores are unsound."}}
{:event/id "38e6592e-70e6-4953-bfaa-8a8a7fd08f54" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:fa5c14d5-c1dd-4779-a3f2-d0189d168caa" :event/seq 2 :event/causes ["e8f6b830-e4ce-4011-837b-72327b2996a2"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:fa5c14d5-c1dd-4779-a3f2-d0189d168caa" :event/at "2026-09-09T13:49:36Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/temp-memory-failover-is-best-effort-not-coherent :finding/shapes #{:store :cache :infra} :finding/current-name "temp-memory primary Mongo + process-local fallback" :finding/candidate-name "BestEffortFailoverStore<Primary,Fallback>" :finding/claim "Temporary memory uses Mongo when available and a process-local TTL map otherwise, but successful primary writes and deletes do not mirror or invalidate fallback state, while reads fall through on a falsey or absent primary result. Local reads also require a truthy stored value. The fallback therefore provides best-effort availability for ephemeral scratch state, not coherent cache, mirror, write-through, or arbitrary-value store semantics."}}
{:event/id "d57390b5-a519-4ad7-be8e-94703b4382d8" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:fa5c14d5-c1dd-4779-a3f2-d0189d168caa" :event/seq 3 :event/causes ["38e6592e-70e6-4953-bfaa-8a8a7fd08f54"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:fa5c14d5-c1dd-4779-a3f2-d0189d168caa" :event/at "2026-09-09T13:49:36Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/fallback-admission-belongs-to-capability-contract :finding/shapes #{:protocol :store :law} :finding/current-name "temp-memory fallback versus translation-evidence/OpenPlanner refusal" :finding/candidate-name "FallbackAdmission<Capability,LossModel>" :finding/claim "Knoxx permits local fallback for short-lived temporary memory, but the translation-evidence registry explicitly refuses in-memory substitution when durable revision-bound receipts are unavailable, and OpenPlanner projection repair uses a separate capability protocol so callers can reject an unsupported selected client before falling back to a different store. Fallback eligibility is therefore part of the capability's authority and loss model, not a generic infrastructure policy."}}
